<title>USA: Rhone-Poulenc says FDA clears Centeon.</title>
<headline>Rhone-Poulenc says FDA clears Centeon.</headline>
<dateline>COLLEGEVILLE, Pa. 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rhone-Poulenc Rorer Inc, the global pharmaceutical company, said Thursday its Centeon joint venture with Hoechst AG has received federal regulatory clearance to distribute biological products made at its Kankakee, Ill., facility.</p>
<p>The distribution is subject to the normal industry practice of lot-release testing by the Food and Drug Administration before distribution, Rhone-Poulenc said.</p>
<p>It said Centeon expects to submit newly manufactured biological products to the FDA for lot release in the next few weeks.</p>
</text>
